asr-002119
02:01:08.940 --> 02:01:20.940
PhilHealth President and CEO Dr. Beverly Lorraine Ho: So, that should hopefully be in place kasi for this whole year, nag-start na po mag-collect ng data, more data yung PhilHealth sa mga healthcare provider, yung CF5 po.

asr-002120
02:01:20.940 --> 02:01:25.940
PhilHealth President and CEO Dr. Beverly Lorraine Ho: So, yun po yung magiging basis namin para po maglagay ng mga adjustments for...

asr-002121
02:01:26.160 --> 02:01:28.480
PhilHealth President and CEO Dr. Beverly Lorraine Ho: the cases po. Thank you, sir.

asr-002122
02:01:28.660 --> 02:01:31.040
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: Okay. Thank you very much, sir.

asr-002123
02:01:31.580 --> 02:01:36.200
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: Maraming salamat po, Congressman Marlo Bancoro, for your questions.

asr-002124
02:01:37.880 --> 02:01:51.320
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: Next, we will go back to the minority. May we recognize the Honorable Deputy Minority Leader, Representative Antonio Quino.

asr-002125
02:01:52.180 --> 02:01:53.800
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: Sir, you have five minutes.

asr-002126
02:01:53.800 --> 02:01:55.600
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Thank you, Chair.

asr-002127
02:01:56.160 --> 02:02:06.860
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ang mga tanong po natin, may kinalaman sa budget cuts sa DOH-retained hospitals and also sa mga GOCC hospitals.

asr-002128
02:02:07.340 --> 02:02:09.120
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Doon muna sa DOH-retained hospitals.

asr-002129
02:02:09.920 --> 02:02:21.100
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Alam po natin na matindi ang problema ng shortage ng staff, hospital staff, doctor, nurse, support staff, etc.

asr-002130
02:02:21.540 --> 02:02:25.100
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Pero nagtataka po tayo, first slide, bakit po...

asr-002131
02:02:26.160 --> 02:02:34.040
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: May mga DOH hospitals na may mga substantial cuts sa kanilang personnel services budget.

asr-002132
02:02:34.800 --> 02:02:39.020
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Kulang na nga ng staff, binawasan pa. Ano pong explanation?

asr-002133
02:02:46.350 --> 02:02:47.870
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: DOH, please reply.

asr-002134
02:02:50.030 --> 02:03:01.190
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Ang ano po namin, kasi nga po nagkaroon ng guidance na yung JO na unfilled will not be allowed to be filled up for 2026 and 2027.

asr-002135
02:03:01.930 --> 02:03:02.550
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Maaring yun.

asr-002136
02:03:02.590 --> 02:03:12.230
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Pagkakaalam po yung difference. Pero yung PS po, sa pagkakaalam ko, hindi naman po yung actual filled up position po naman ay hindi nabawasan.

asr-002137
02:03:13.770 --> 02:03:17.310
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Well, yung JO sa MOE po yun, ano.

asr-002138
02:03:18.110 --> 02:03:21.470
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Pero eto nga, there are some significant...

asr-002139
02:03:21.470 --> 02:03:25.630
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: For example, Quirino Medical Center, binawasan ng...

asr-002140
02:03:25.630 --> 02:03:27.250
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Binawasan na... Sorry.

asr-002141
02:03:28.130 --> 02:03:30.630
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Yung pinakamalaki...

asr-002142
02:03:30.630 --> 02:03:31.990
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Rizal Medical Center.

asr-002143
02:03:32.590 --> 02:03:36.210
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Binawasan ng halos 10%, 8% yung kanilang PS.

asr-002144
02:03:37.370 --> 02:03:40.130
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ibig po ba sabihin nito, nagbawas ng personnel?

asr-002145
02:03:44.170 --> 02:03:47.330
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: 112 million pesos ang binawas.

asr-002146
02:03:54.550 --> 02:03:56.930
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Yung ano daw po, nag-scrap and build.

asr-002147
02:03:57.030 --> 02:04:06.050
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Yung mga unfilled position po ay hindi na naisama dun sa subsequent posting ng ating 2027.

asr-002148
02:04:06.390 --> 02:04:08.150
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: But the numbers are still the same.

asr-002149
02:04:08.310 --> 02:04:13.190
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, nagbawas ng admin position.

asr-002150
02:04:13.370 --> 02:04:14.830
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Positions, ganun po ba?

asr-002151
02:04:20.970 --> 02:04:26.410
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: I may request sa Mr. Chair, yung ating pong USEC for admin and finance.

asr-002152
02:04:27.190 --> 02:04:27.670
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: Good morning po.

asr-002153
02:04:27.670 --> 02:04:29.650
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: USEC for finance is recognized.

asr-002154
02:04:30.030 --> 02:04:31.830
DOH Undersecretary Maylene M. Beltran: Good morning po, Mr. Chair.

asr-002155
02:04:32.350 --> 02:04:32.570
DOH Undersecretary Maylene M. Beltran: Yes.

asr-002156
02:04:32.890 --> 02:04:38.250
DOH Undersecretary Maylene M. Beltran: Yung bawas po dyan, Kong, ay because of the unfilled positions.

asr-002157
02:04:38.870 --> 02:04:43.370
DOH Undersecretary Maylene M. Beltran: But the overall total of plantilla positions remain the same.

asr-002158
02:04:44.190 --> 02:04:45.370
DOH Undersecretary Maylene M. Beltran: So, yan lang po kasi.

asr-002159
02:04:45.570 --> 02:04:46.650
DOH Undersecretary Maylene M. Beltran: Yung hindi pa...

asr-002160
02:04:46.650 --> 02:04:48.390
DOH Undersecretary Maylene M. Beltran: Na-fulfill upon for this year.

asr-002161
02:04:49.610 --> 02:04:51.670
DOH Undersecretary Maylene M. Beltran: Yun po yung explanation po, Mr. Chair.

asr-002162
02:04:52.190 --> 02:04:54.630
DOH Undersecretary Maylene M. Beltran: So, yung mga unfilled nyo, tinanggal na.

asr-002163
02:04:55.250 --> 02:04:57.330
DOH Undersecretary Maylene M. Beltran: So, nabawasan kayo ng plantilla positions.

asr-002164
02:04:58.150 --> 02:05:05.550
DOH Undersecretary Maylene M. Beltran: Mr. Chair, hindi po mababawasan yung total plantilla positions po.

asr-002165
02:05:05.750 --> 02:05:12.330
DOH Undersecretary Maylene M. Beltran: Only the difference would be explained by the fact that these are already, as of now, unfilled positions.

asr-002166
02:05:13.770 --> 02:05:16.530
DOH Undersecretary Maylene M. Beltran: So, ibabalik din po as soon as these are filled.

asr-002167
02:05:16.650 --> 02:05:19.130
DOH Undersecretary Maylene M. Beltran: Sa original na amount po.

asr-002168
02:05:19.530 --> 02:05:22.720
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, binawasan nga?

asr-002169
02:05:29.500 --> 02:05:39.960
DOH Undersecretary Maylene M. Beltran: Sir, kung nabawasan po talaga, however, pwede hong mag-supplemental budget po during that time na ma-fill upon na po yung position.

asr-002170
02:05:41.560 --> 02:05:43.980
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Sorry, what do you mean by supplemental budget?

asr-002171
02:05:44.120 --> 02:05:45.500
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Congress po ang gumagawa nun.

asr-002172
02:05:48.520 --> 02:05:52.860
DOH Undersecretary Maylene M. Beltran: Sir, isasama rin po sa ating mga...

asr-002173
02:05:52.860 --> 02:05:56.860
DOH Undersecretary Maylene M. Beltran: the total budget request for those hospitals.

asr-002174
02:05:56.860 --> 02:06:07.040
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: That means, binawasan kayo for next fiscal year and then in 2028, pwede kayong mag-request ulit.

asr-002175
02:06:07.620 --> 02:06:18.480
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, ang concern natin ay kulang na nga tapos kayong tinanggalan pa kayo ng additional plantilla positions.

asr-002176
02:06:18.640 --> 02:06:22.860
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: That means, you have no opportunity to fill them up during the fiscal year.

asr-002177
02:06:25.160 --> 02:06:26.220
DOH Undersecretary Maylene M. Beltran: Sir, pwede pa po.

asr-002178
02:06:26.220 --> 02:06:30.520
DOH Undersecretary Maylene M. Beltran: So, in short, sir, hindi ho talaga bawas yung budget.

asr-002179
02:06:30.540 --> 02:06:31.920
DOH Undersecretary Maylene M. Beltran: For personal services.

asr-002180
02:06:32.720 --> 02:06:38.340
DOH Undersecretary Maylene M. Beltran: Only, again, the difference is explained by the fact that these have been unfilled positions.

asr-002181
02:06:39.040 --> 02:06:43.140
DOH Undersecretary Maylene M. Beltran: But the total budget po for personal services would remain the same.

asr-002182
02:06:47.070 --> 02:06:49.030
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Mr. Chen, naubos yung oras dito.

asr-002183
02:06:49.210 --> 02:06:56.670
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Pwede po bang magbigay ng written explanation yung DOH sa nangyayari sa pagbawas?

asr-002184
02:06:56.930 --> 02:06:57.870
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: May bawas eh.

asr-002185
02:06:58.270 --> 02:06:59.850
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Tapos sinasabi, walang nabawasan.

asr-002186
02:07:00.850 --> 02:07:02.790
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: And explanation na rin kung bakit.

asr-002187
02:07:02.790 --> 02:07:03.590
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ano bang problema?

asr-002188
02:07:04.050 --> 02:07:07.210
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Can I hear lang, bakit ba hindi ma-fill up yung unfilled positions?

asr-002189
02:07:07.590 --> 02:07:09.530
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: What are the nature of these positions and why?

asr-002190
02:07:11.070 --> 02:07:13.890
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Sabantala, puro J-O-N-C-O-S naman kayo.

asr-002191
02:07:15.690 --> 02:07:29.130
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: So, the DOH requested to answer in written form para comprehensive at maintindihan ni Rep. Tino talaga yung inyong sagot dun sa napakahalagang katanungan.

asr-002192
02:07:29.470 --> 02:07:29.890
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: Yes, sir.

asr-002193
02:07:29.890 --> 02:07:31.490
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: Para hindi na rin maubos ang oras.

asr-002194
02:07:32.230 --> 02:07:32.750
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: Please.

asr-002195
02:07:32.790 --> 02:07:34.710
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: Please pause the time.

asr-002196
02:07:35.690 --> 02:07:36.850
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: I-restore niyo po.

asr-002197
02:07:37.010 --> 02:07:39.390
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: Dahil hindi na po nagtatanong si Rep. Tino.

asr-002198
02:07:39.850 --> 02:07:42.950
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: Please restore the time of Rep. Tino.

asr-002199
02:07:43.150 --> 02:07:45.370
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: So, sulat na lang po para mas comprehensive.

asr-002200
02:07:46.130 --> 02:07:47.530
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: Tapos, restore yung time.

asr-002201
02:07:47.530 --> 02:07:48.630
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Could we just briefly hear kung bakit.

asr-002202
02:07:48.950 --> 02:07:50.490
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Anong problema sa unfilled position?

asr-002203
02:07:50.990 --> 02:07:51.890
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Please reply.

asr-002204
02:07:55.050 --> 02:07:59.750
DOH Undersecretary Maylene M. Beltran: Sir, yung mga unfilled positions po would be for various reasons.

asr-002205
02:07:59.750 --> 02:08:04.110
DOH Undersecretary Maylene M. Beltran: Number one po, may mga positions na there are no takers.

asr-002206
02:08:04.110 --> 02:08:11.930
DOH Undersecretary Maylene M. Beltran: Especially those medical positions which would have more competitive salaries elsewhere.

asr-002207
02:08:12.490 --> 02:08:20.110
DOH Undersecretary Maylene M. Beltran: Number two, yung mga may ibang hospitals po na yung ibang positions are really for residencies and fellowships.

asr-002208
02:08:21.070 --> 02:08:27.770
DOH Undersecretary Maylene M. Beltran: That's why they are not filled up permanently because these are temporary in nature.

asr-002209
02:08:27.770 --> 02:08:29.510
DOH Undersecretary Maylene M. Beltran: Yun po, sir.

asr-002210
02:08:29.630 --> 02:08:33.770
DOH Undersecretary Maylene M. Beltran: Yung ibang mga reasons for unfilled.

asr-002211
02:08:34.110 --> 02:08:35.210
DOH Undersecretary Maylene M. Beltran: Posing up of positions.

asr-002212
02:08:35.610 --> 02:08:39.010
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ano yung mga position na hindi competitive kaya hindi na-fill up?

asr-002213
02:08:39.770 --> 02:08:45.650
DOH Undersecretary Maylene M. Beltran: Sir, mga physical therapies, development, speech therapies, etc. po.

asr-002214
02:08:46.350 --> 02:08:46.870
DOH Undersecretary Maylene M. Beltran: Especially.

asr-002215
02:08:47.790 --> 02:08:50.690
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, isama na po yun sa isasubmit.

asr-002216
02:08:50.810 --> 02:08:52.810
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ano yung mga nature at anong problema?

asr-002217
02:08:52.950 --> 02:08:54.650
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Masyadong mababa ba yung sweldo?

asr-002218
02:08:54.850 --> 02:08:57.030
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, dapat i-address and so on.

asr-002219
02:08:57.570 --> 02:08:57.790
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Okay.

asr-002220
02:08:58.270 --> 02:08:59.090
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: Mr. Chair, thank you.

asr-002221
02:08:59.090 --> 02:08:59.550
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: Now, next slide.

asr-002222
02:08:59.550 --> 02:09:01.950
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: Pakitulat na lang po yung comprehensive answer.

asr-002223
02:09:02.350 --> 02:09:02.670
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: Thank you.

asr-002224
02:09:02.670 --> 02:09:03.810
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Next slide, Rep. Tino.

asr-002225
02:09:03.930 --> 02:09:04.070
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Please.

asr-002226
02:09:04.110 --> 02:09:04.930
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Please proceed.

asr-002227
02:09:05.150 --> 02:09:06.310
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Cut to MOE.

asr-002228
02:09:06.510 --> 02:09:12.130
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, again, alam natin napakalala ng problema ng sitwasyon sa mga public hospitals.

asr-002229
02:09:13.950 --> 02:09:16.710
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: They have to make do with limited budget.

asr-002230
02:09:16.890 --> 02:09:23.290
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ngayon, nagtataka tayo bakit in many DOH hospitals, binawasan pa.

asr-002231
02:09:24.430 --> 02:09:27.410
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: In some cases, napakalaki ng binawas sa kanilang MOE.

asr-002232
02:09:27.410 --> 02:09:33.510
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Again, Irino Memorial Medical Center, binawasan ng half a billion pesos.

asr-002233
02:09:33.510 --> 02:09:43.190
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Yung kanilang MOE, isang example lang yun, National Center for Mental Health, 311 million cut in MOE.

asr-002234
02:09:43.390 --> 02:09:44.030
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Please explain.

asr-002235
02:09:52.120 --> 02:09:57.660
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Habang merong policy ng zero balance billing, libre, babawasan naman yung MOE.

asr-002236
02:09:57.800 --> 02:09:58.140
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Paano yun?

asr-002237
02:10:05.020 --> 02:10:11.980
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Mr. Chair, ito po ay sa DOH Regional Hospitals, bukod pa po itong specialty hospitals.

asr-002238
02:10:12.460 --> 02:10:13.400
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Ikinukuha lang yan.

asr-002239
02:10:14.260 --> 02:10:16.820
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Doon po naman sa aming...

asr-002240
02:10:16.820 --> 02:10:28.240
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Dito po sa ating mga regional hospitals, ang aming GAA noong 2026 ay 101.7, ang NEPO ay 102.9.

asr-002241
02:10:28.320 --> 02:10:35.200
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: So, yun po ay for regional hospitals ng DOH ay tumaas po ng 1.1%.

asr-002242
02:10:35.200 --> 02:10:46.380
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Pero yung operations of DOH hospitals in Metro Manila, yun po yung bumaba from 30 billion noong 2026 GAA to 26.9 billion,

asr-002243
02:10:46.500 --> 02:10:48.480
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: which is lower than 10.2%.

asr-002244
02:10:48.480 --> 02:11:05.860
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Ah, anong reason? Yung, although ang hiningi po namin ay 31.7 po para nga po to cover our projected MOOE, pero nag-grant lang po ay 26.9.

asr-002244-split-2
02:11:05.860 --> 02:11:19.810
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, bakit nga po, nakita ko, Batanes Provincial General Hospital, ang chairman ng health, galing sa

asr-002246
02:11:19.830 --> 02:11:49.720
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Batanes, binawasan din ang MOE. So, wala kayong explanation. Is it a DBM matter? Then, Chair, can we ask the DBM, yung representative dito ng DBM, bakit binawasan yung MOE ng mga ospital na ito? E gipit na gipit na nga. Is the representative of DBM present? May taga-DBM po ba na nandito ngayon? Ayun.

asr-002246-split-2
02:11:49.720 --> 02:11:54.800
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: Quick interjection, Mr. Chair, if the honorable, my very good friend, Hon. Tinio will allow.

asr-002247
02:11:54.800 --> 02:11:56.900
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: Please proceed.

asr-002247-split-2
02:11:56.900 --> 02:12:24.780
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: Yes, thank you very much, Mr. Chair. In relation to the question of the Honorable Tinio, may I also propose that the Department of Health furnish the Committee on Appropriations a copy of the field health reimbursements of each hospital, as well as medical assistance program allocation of each hospital, including the actual utilization of their MOOE because this might be the reason

asr-002248
02:12:24.780 --> 02:12:39.920
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: why there was a cut in their MOOE because there was a higher allocation of MAIFIP as well as PhilHealth reimbursements. I so move, Mr. Chair. And thank you very much, Congressman Tolosa.

asr-002248-split-2
02:12:39.920 --> 02:12:41.760
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: Congressman Tinio!

asr-002248-split-3
02:12:41.760 --> 02:12:48.160
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: Sorry, Mr. Chair. Congressman Tinio, my very good friend.

asr-002248-split-4
02:12:48.160 --> 02:12:54.760
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: I believe that was a motion, DS. Yes. Are there any seconds?

asr-002249
02:12:54.760 --> 02:12:56.030
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: I second that.

asr-002249-split-2
02:12:56.030 --> 02:13:03.090
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Sige. Okay. Pero gusto pa rin po natin marinig, ano yung justification for cutting the MOOE of these DOH hospitals?

asr-002249-split-3
02:13:03.090 --> 02:13:12.750
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: So the documents are requested to be submitted para makita rin po natin.

asr-002249-split-3-split-2
02:13:12.750 --> 02:13:17.580
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Wala po ba yung DBM dito? Ah, nandiyan na ba? Alam ko meron.

asr-002249-split-3-split-2-split-2
02:13:17.580 --> 02:13:22.410
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: Ayan, katabi niyo. Ah, please reply to the question of Congressman Tinio.

asr-002249-split-4
02:13:22.410 --> 02:13:26.470
DBM Official: Yes po, good morning po, Mr. Chair, Your Honor. Ah, actually po yung

asr-002250
02:13:26.470 --> 02:13:56.520
DBM Official: MOE naman po ng hospitals for DOH, we just follow naman po yung normative financing as provided din naman po by the DOH. And sila rin po yung nagbe-break ng MOE requirements. So, there may have, meron pong mga nag-decrease nga po from the 2026. But this is based naman po sa normative financing. And additionally, as mentioned nga din po ni Secretary kanina, a portion po, meron

asr-002251
02:13:56.520 --> 02:14:35.140
DBM Official: pong portion na nailagay sa PhilHealth to implement the CBB, implementation of the CBB, which will eventually rin naman po is papasok din sa mga, as additional MOE po ng mga hospitals. So, yun po yung naging policy for the 2027 budget na ang tingin po kasi is sectoral nga po yung tingin natin ngayon, not just yung sa DOH lang, kasama po yung sa PhilHealth dahil nga po mayroon nga po doon na dagdag na around 14 billion to implement din po yung CBB po ng DOH. Thank you po.

asr-002252
02:14:35.140 --> 02:15:00.000
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Could we have a response from the DOH Secretary on that? Parang nagtuturuan. Una, sabi nila, well, binatay lang namin sa sinubmit niyo. Pangalawa, the other one is binawasan yung MOE dahil mababawi naman sa PhilHealth through the ZBB, zero balance billing. Could we have a response?

asr-002259
02:15:00.000 --> 02:15:01.880
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Di ba may problema doon?

asr-002260
02:15:02.920 --> 02:15:05.280
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Please reply, Sec. Mercado.

asr-002261
02:15:05.360 --> 02:15:09.060
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: So, all the OH hospitals are allowed income retention.

asr-002262
02:15:09.480 --> 02:15:15.260
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: So, as mentioned earlier by Kong Garin, we should look at it in totality.

asr-002263
02:15:16.400 --> 02:15:21.640
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Kung makano po yung iba pang revenue from PhilHealth from Ma'a-Ethip.

asr-002264
02:15:22.080 --> 02:15:26.200
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Kasi nga po, ang understanding ko nung kami po ay nag-usap ni Sec. Kim,

asr-002265
02:15:26.200 --> 02:15:29.680
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: ma-iwasan po din yung tinatawag na double financing.

asr-002266
02:15:30.420 --> 02:15:36.440
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Meron na po tayong coverage through GAA, pero meron pa rin revenue stream from other sources.

asr-002267
02:15:37.620 --> 02:15:42.740
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Kaya po, gaya po na nasabi ng ating representative from DBM,

asr-002268
02:15:43.100 --> 02:15:49.660
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: it's a sector approach na parang in a way itong kabuan,

asr-002269
02:15:50.240 --> 02:15:55.840
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: pero parang it's a left-pocket, right-pocket transaction as it pertains to PhilHealth.

asr-002270
02:15:55.840 --> 02:16:03.840
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Baka yun po yung kailangang kuntingnan din at bibigay po nga po namin yung ating datos dito po as requested po.

asr-002271
02:16:05.260 --> 02:16:06.200
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Please continue.

asr-002272
02:16:06.740 --> 02:16:13.260
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Mr. Secretary, hindi po ba problema to na binabawasan na yung MOE?

asr-002273
02:16:13.480 --> 02:16:17.980
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Anyway, ang sabi nyo, mababawi naman sa Ma'a-Ethip or sa PhilHealth.

asr-002274
02:16:18.480 --> 02:16:23.720
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Yung mga reimbursement, buti kong instantaneous ang reimbursement.

asr-002275
02:16:23.720 --> 02:16:25.720
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: In the meantime, the hospital...

asr-002276
02:16:25.840 --> 02:16:28.400
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Well, we'll have to operate based on the available funds.

asr-002277
02:16:29.520 --> 02:16:30.320
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: E paano na ngayon yan?

asr-002278
02:16:30.420 --> 02:16:32.260
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: E di wala silang kapos ang pondo.

asr-002279
02:16:35.140 --> 02:16:42.040
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Is that a fair characterization of the situation?

asr-002280
02:16:42.240 --> 02:16:46.400
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Is that fair to yung mga pasyente, mga kababayan natin?

asr-002281
02:16:47.380 --> 02:16:48.200
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Hindi ba problema yun?

asr-002282
02:16:49.540 --> 02:16:52.340
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Medyo nga po may impact in terms of the cash flow.

asr-002283
02:16:52.560 --> 02:16:55.280
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Pero ang ating nga pong next step,

asr-002284
02:16:55.840 --> 02:16:58.180
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: progress po tayo doon sa tinatawag na global payment.

asr-002285
02:16:58.360 --> 02:17:04.740
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Kung saan po naka-estimate na magkano po yung mga services na i-re-render po ng ating hospital.

asr-002286
02:17:05.160 --> 02:17:08.500
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: At ifo, front load na po ng PhilHealth yun sa ating mga hospital.

asr-002287
02:17:11.290 --> 02:17:12.090
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Okay, malinaw, sir.

asr-002288
02:17:12.150 --> 02:17:19.410
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ang kailangan, yung pera, direct ang nasa hospital para direct ang mabigay yung servisyo.

asr-002289
02:17:19.570 --> 02:17:20.830
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Hindi yung...

asr-002290
02:17:20.830 --> 02:17:23.530
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Usually, anong sinasabi ng mga hospital?

asr-002291
02:17:23.530 --> 02:17:25.690
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Sorry, wala kami yan. Bumili kayo sa labas.

asr-002292
02:17:26.070 --> 02:17:27.190
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Di ba, ganun ang nangyayari?

asr-002293
02:17:27.630 --> 02:17:30.190
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: O, dahil kulang ang budget nila.

asr-002294
02:17:32.640 --> 02:17:43.600
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, chair, again, at tinututulan po natin yung ganitong kalakaran na mukhang pinagkakasunduan ng DBM at DOH ngayon na

asr-002295
02:17:43.600 --> 02:17:53.260
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: dahil meron naman daw MyFIP, meron namang PhilHealth, bawasan na natin yung MOOE ng mga hospital.

asr-002296
02:17:53.820 --> 02:17:57.020
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Kailangan po, tiyaki, nandyan ready ang pondo.

asr-002297
02:17:57.020 --> 02:17:58.760
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: My last question.

asr-002298
02:17:59.200 --> 02:18:00.020
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Mr. Chair.

asr-002299
02:18:00.060 --> 02:18:00.560
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: Please proceed.

asr-002300
02:18:00.800 --> 02:18:01.040
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Opo.

asr-002301
02:18:01.400 --> 02:18:03.000
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ay, ano po ang...

asr-002302
02:18:03.000 --> 02:18:07.020
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: I mean, malinaw po na kulang ang ating capacity.

asr-002303
02:18:07.180 --> 02:18:08.300
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: In the end, bed capacity.

asr-002304
02:18:08.460 --> 02:18:14.480
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: You mentioned DOH hospitals have, was it 23,000 total bed capacity?

asr-002305
02:18:14.640 --> 02:18:19.160
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Pero, ang karanasan ng mga kababayan natin, talagang punong-puno.

asr-002306
02:18:20.520 --> 02:18:28.340
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Lalo pa, pag may mga surge during leptospirosis or dengue and so on, punong-puno ang mga hospital, ang mga ward.

asr-002307
02:18:28.340 --> 02:18:30.480
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Mga emergency room, ginagawang ward.

asr-002308
02:18:31.620 --> 02:18:44.580
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ano po ang ginagawa nyo at nasaan sa budget na ito, yung programa para sa expansion of bed capacity ng mga DOH hospitals?

asr-002309
02:18:45.200 --> 02:18:48.540
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ano yung achievement ng administrasyong ito?

asr-002310
02:18:49.140 --> 02:18:55.600
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: How many beds have been added to the DOH hospitals by this administration?

asr-002311
02:18:55.600 --> 02:18:57.600
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: At, for the...

asr-002312
02:18:58.340 --> 02:19:05.020
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: For the proposed year, next year, ilan ang dadagdag pa na bed capacity?

asr-002313
02:19:06.080 --> 02:19:08.960
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: At, meron ba tayong plano in the first place para dito?

asr-002314
02:19:11.440 --> 02:19:19.980
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Mr. Chair, yung akin pong immediate na pwedeng gawin, kasi may lead time din po yung construction, is really efficiencies.

asr-002315
02:19:20.400 --> 02:19:25.740
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Ngayon, ang nasabi ko, kung ma-reduce po natin yung average length of stay, dahil mas maganda po yung treatment,

asr-002316
02:19:25.740 --> 02:19:29.940
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: ay in effect, kung ano po yung reduction dun sa tagal.

asr-002317
02:19:30.040 --> 02:19:35.700
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Kung ano po na tumatagal yung ating pasyente sa hospital, ay parang katumbas na rin ang karagdagang beds po yun.

asr-002318
02:19:36.100 --> 02:19:44.020
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Pero, ang isa pa rin po namin ginagawa sa tulong po ng PhilHealth, ay magkaroon din po ng parang inter-referral system.

asr-002319
02:19:44.440 --> 02:19:53.120
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Yun naman po yung nakasaad dito sa ating UHC law, kung saan din po magtatap na tayo dun sa local government unit hospitals at saka mga private hospitals.

asr-002320
02:19:53.120 --> 02:19:58.400
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: So, meron na po tayong talagang tinatakda na number of beds.

asr-002321
02:19:58.720 --> 02:19:59.120
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: At, meron na po mga...

asr-002322
02:20:00.040 --> 02:20:02.040
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: ng hospital na nag-land 10% of their beds.

asr-002323
02:20:02.520 --> 02:20:13.080
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Na pagka meron pong apaw dito sa ating, in spite of all the efficiencies, ay pwede rin na po natin gamitin yung mga NBB beds na mga private hospital.

asr-002324
02:20:13.960 --> 02:20:22.300
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Although, yun po ay mga short, ang matagalan po talaga, i-expand po yung actual physical plant ng mga DOH hospitals.

asr-002325
02:20:23.560 --> 02:20:24.820
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: So, thank you.

asr-002326
02:20:25.180 --> 02:20:29.820
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Although, in short, Mr. Chair, ang intindi ko lang sa sagot ay walang plano ang DOH.

asr-002327
02:20:30.040 --> 02:20:39.860
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Sa kagyat, and maybe until the end of the administration, walang sistematikong plano para ma-expand yung bed capacity ng mga DOH hospitals.

asr-002328
02:20:40.980 --> 02:20:49.600
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Yun ang dinig ko. Sabi, must focus on efficiencies and maybe distribute to the local hospitals and so on.

asr-002329
02:20:50.240 --> 02:20:55.920
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, well, we will take this up further. Tingin natin may problema yan.

asr-002330
02:20:55.920 --> 02:20:59.920
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: No? Dahil, yun ang pangunahing...

asr-002331
02:21:00.040 --> 02:21:10.680
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Maganda, merong zero balance billing program, pero kung limitado ang kapasidad, ay limitado ang makikinabang na mamamayan natin,

asr-002332
02:21:11.340 --> 02:21:15.960
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: at inevitably, ipapasa sila sa private sector na mas mahal.

asr-002333
02:21:16.860 --> 02:21:29.100
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Follow up ko na lang po, please submit a report on this administration's achievements in expanding capacity and any plans, kung meron man,

asr-002334
02:21:29.100 --> 02:21:30.020
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: in that program.

asr-002335
02:21:30.040 --> 02:21:31.580
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: With that regard, thank you po.

asr-002336
02:21:31.980 --> 02:21:33.180
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Yes, maraming salamat.

asr-002337
02:21:33.200 --> 02:21:34.160
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Can I do that, Mr. Jointer?

asr-002338
02:21:34.160 --> 02:21:35.160
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Yes, last reply ni Secretary.

asr-002339
02:21:35.160 --> 02:21:36.560
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Nakuha ko na po yung datos.

asr-002340
02:21:36.880 --> 02:21:45.620
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Ang amin pong estimate, yung kasalukuyan pong bed capacity ay 30,000, ay aakyat po ng 45,000 by 2028.

asr-002341
02:21:46.040 --> 02:21:48.900
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: So, meron naman pong program. Isasama na lang po namin.

asr-002342
02:21:48.900 --> 02:21:51.360
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Sir, pakiulit lang po. By 2028?

asr-002343
02:21:52.080 --> 02:21:59.360
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Current po na authorized bed capacity po, ngayon, noong 2025 na 30,000, ay aakyat po ng 45,000.

asr-002344
02:22:00.040 --> 02:22:11.080
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, in two years, ay dadagdagan niyo by 15,000 yung bed capacity ng mga DOH hospitals.

asr-002345
02:22:12.080 --> 02:22:15.780
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: That's an important statement.

asr-002346
02:22:15.780 --> 02:22:19.500
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Please clarify, sir, para mas maintindihan po ng committee.

asr-002347
02:22:20.140 --> 02:22:26.400
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: At parang reflected ba sa budget yan? You have only until 27-28.

asr-002348
02:22:26.960 --> 02:22:33.620
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Naka-reflect naman po dun sa budget ng expansion.

asr-002349
02:22:33.680 --> 02:22:44.600
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: At yun nga lang po, dahil nag-cut dun sa HVEP, medyo maka-ma-delay ng konti dito sa target.

asr-002350
02:22:44.760 --> 02:22:48.820
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Unless nga po ma-reinstate natin yung ating pong hinihingi ng allocation.

asr-002351
02:22:49.240 --> 02:22:49.720
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Mr. Chair?

asr-002352
02:22:50.420 --> 02:22:51.740
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: Tin-report na lang, Chair. Thank you.

asr-002353
02:22:51.740 --> 02:22:59.880
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: So, sek, paki yung comprehensive answer sa mga questions ni DML Tino.

asr-002354
02:23:00.340 --> 02:23:02.740
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: At yung motion ni DS Garibaldi.

asr-002355
02:23:03.680 --> 02:23:10.540
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: Pa rin, pakisagot po in written form para mas ma-appreciate ng committee and its members.

asr-002356
02:23:11.180 --> 02:23:14.680
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: Nang sa ganun, ay mas mapaliwanag natin ng mas maigi.

asr-002357
02:23:14.680 --> 02:23:19.940
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: And I understand yung efficiencies na sinasabi siguro ni Secretary.

asr-002358
02:23:20.560 --> 02:23:25.980
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: Yung bylaw, kailangan pati yung private hospital mag-create ng 10% ward.

asr-002359
02:23:26.740 --> 02:23:31.500
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: Kung magagawa ito, that will expand the bed capacity.

asr-002360
02:23:31.500 --> 02:23:38.940
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: Not only of the government hospital, pero magagamit natin yung existing facilities din ng private hospital.

asr-002361
02:23:39.220 --> 02:23:45.640
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: So, malaking bagay yung paki-explain din po sa inyong written answers.

asr-002362
02:23:46.440 --> 02:23:51.800
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: So, thank you very much, DML Tino, for your questions and queries.

asr-002363
02:23:52.540 --> 02:23:58.600
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: Rest assured, ipapasa po natin yung mga sagot ng DOH and PhilHealth sa committee at sa inyo po.

asr-002364
02:23:59.600 --> 02:24:00.620
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: Okay, so.

asr-002365
02:24:01.500 --> 02:24:03.440
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: Next, we go back to the majority.

asr-002366
02:24:05.040 --> 02:24:11.520
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: May we call on our Deputy Speaker, Ferge Biron, for his questions.

asr-002367
02:24:11.520 --> 02:24:12.820
Deputy Speaker Ferjenel G. Biron, M.D.: Thank you, Mr. Chairman.

asr-002368
02:24:13.520 --> 02:24:20.400
Deputy Speaker Ferjenel G. Biron, M.D.: First of all, let me congratulate Secretary Mercado and Dr. Ho for your respective appointments.

asr-002369
02:24:21.820 --> 02:24:27.920
Deputy Speaker Ferjenel G. Biron, M.D.: So, while I was observing the interpellation of Congressman Tino,

asr-002370
02:24:28.720 --> 02:24:31.280
Deputy Speaker Ferjenel G. Biron, M.D.: I observed that the good Secretary,

asr-002371
02:24:31.500 --> 02:24:40.820
Deputy Speaker Ferjenel G. Biron, M.D.: he has some difficulty struggling on issues pertaining to the budget of the DOH.

asr-002372
02:24:41.400 --> 02:24:42.860
Deputy Speaker Ferjenel G. Biron, M.D.: May I know from the Secretary,

asr-002373
02:24:43.520 --> 02:24:50.580
Deputy Speaker Ferjenel G. Biron, M.D.: if this budget is your own doing or is a budget formulated by your predecessor?

asr-002374
02:24:53.250 --> 02:24:57.910
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: When I came, Mr. Chairman, I came in po na meron na pong approval yung NEP.

asr-002375
02:24:57.910 --> 02:25:02.930
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: So, it's already, kumbaga, the budget from, yes.

asr-002376
02:25:03.170 --> 02:25:06.850
Deputy Speaker Ferjenel G. Biron, M.D.: Yes, very obvious naman siya eh, na hindi niyo budget ito eh.

asr-002377
02:25:07.990 --> 02:25:12.690
Deputy Speaker Ferjenel G. Biron, M.D.: So, I would suggest, this representation would like to suggest to the Secretary,

asr-002378
02:25:13.490 --> 02:25:16.130
Deputy Speaker Ferjenel G. Biron, M.D.: you have to be honest and candid to Congress.

asr-002379
02:25:17.410 --> 02:25:19.890
Deputy Speaker Ferjenel G. Biron, M.D.: Kung meron kang nakita na hindi mo gusto,

asr-002380
02:25:20.730 --> 02:25:23.450
Deputy Speaker Ferjenel G. Biron, M.D.: or gusto mo i-amendahan, or gusto mo dagdagan,

asr-002381
02:25:24.170 --> 02:25:27.970
Deputy Speaker Ferjenel G. Biron, M.D.: sabihin mo sa amin, because we're here to help you and help the Department.

asr-002382
02:25:27.970 --> 02:25:31.470
Deputy Speaker Ferjenel G. Biron, M.D.: So, my first question, Mr. Secretary, is,

asr-002383
02:25:32.030 --> 02:25:32.890
Deputy Speaker Ferjenel G. Biron, M.D.: 10 years ago,

asr-002384
02:25:33.170 --> 02:25:41.950
Deputy Speaker Ferjenel G. Biron, M.D.: the bed-to-patient ratio in the hospital for both government and private hospital is 0.8

asr-002385
02:25:41.950 --> 02:25:44.790
Deputy Speaker Ferjenel G. Biron, M.D.: to 1,000 population.

asr-002386
02:25:47.800 --> 02:25:53.220
Deputy Speaker Ferjenel G. Biron, M.D.: Meaning to say, we have a deficit of around 140,000 beds.

asr-002387
02:25:53.620 --> 02:25:54.960
Deputy Speaker Ferjenel G. Biron, M.D.: That was 10 years ago.

asr-002388
02:25:56.200 --> 02:26:01.740
Deputy Speaker Ferjenel G. Biron, M.D.: So, may I know from the Secretary, what is the present bed-to-patient ratio?

asr-002389
02:26:02.100 --> 02:26:07.460
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: In Metro Manila po, it's 1.7.

asr-002390
02:26:08.100 --> 02:26:14.540
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: So, yun po ay almost compliant to the WHO standard of 3.

asr-002391
02:26:15.540 --> 02:26:22.240
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Overall, nationwide, dahil nga po mas konti yung bed-to-patient ratio sa ating probinsya,

asr-002392
02:26:22.680 --> 02:26:26.500
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: bababa po ng mga 1.1, 1.2.

asr-002393
02:26:27.380 --> 02:26:36.300
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: So, we're still much under the prescribed bed-to-patient ratio provided by WHO.

asr-002394
02:26:36.980 --> 02:26:37.940
Deputy Speaker Ferjenel G. Biron, M.D.: Okay, moving on to the...

asr-002395
02:26:38.100 --> 02:26:40.360
Deputy Speaker Ferjenel G. Biron, M.D.: Next question, Mr. Secretary.

asr-002396
02:26:42.180 --> 02:26:50.860
Deputy Speaker Ferjenel G. Biron, M.D.: I'm sure you're aware that the global benchmark for national expenditure on health is 10% of GDP.

asr-002397
02:26:51.200 --> 02:26:51.960
Deputy Speaker Ferjenel G. Biron, M.D.: Do you agree with me?

asr-002398
02:26:53.420 --> 02:26:56.280
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Yes po, yun po yung standard benchmark.

asr-002399
02:26:56.340 --> 02:26:56.620
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Yes.

asr-002400
02:26:57.160 --> 02:26:59.760
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: But for developing economies like the Philippines,

asr-002401
02:27:00.760 --> 02:27:03.200
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: acceptable na po yung 4 to 5%.

asr-002402
02:27:03.200 --> 02:27:06.640
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: So, given your budget of P353 billion,

asr-002403
02:27:06.640 --> 02:27:07.940
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: that is all...

asr-002404
02:27:07.940 --> 02:27:12.120
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Almost 4.5% of the national budget.

asr-002405
02:27:13.760 --> 02:27:17.600
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Although, when you consider po yung percentage of GDP,

asr-002406
02:27:17.820 --> 02:27:21.640
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: it's a combination po of government and private spending.

asr-002407
02:27:21.640 --> 02:27:27.860
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: So, government right now accounts for 46% of the total healthcare spend.

asr-002408
02:27:27.960 --> 02:27:29.040
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Roughly half.

asr-002409
02:27:29.380 --> 02:27:34.600
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: So, times 2 po, baka abot na po ng 7% kung kasama po yung spending ng mga...

asr-002410
02:27:34.600 --> 02:27:37.220
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: So, aabot tayo ng 7% of GDP.

asr-002411
02:27:37.220 --> 02:27:39.480
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Which is quite acceptable.

asr-002412
02:27:40.380 --> 02:27:43.840
Deputy Speaker Ferjenel G. Biron, M.D.: So, given the scarce resources of the government,

asr-002413
02:27:44.600 --> 02:27:50.700
Deputy Speaker Ferjenel G. Biron, M.D.: your department is beset with a serious problem on expired medicines.

asr-002414
02:27:51.580 --> 02:27:54.400
Deputy Speaker Ferjenel G. Biron, M.D.: Maliit na nga yung ating budget, maliit ang pera natin.

asr-002415
02:27:55.040 --> 02:28:00.020
Deputy Speaker Ferjenel G. Biron, M.D.: Pero marami pa rin ang problema ng DOH sa expired medicines.

asr-002416
02:28:00.020 --> 02:28:06.900
Deputy Speaker Ferjenel G. Biron, M.D.: Can you provide this committee with a report of expired medicines since 2022?

asr-002417
02:28:07.220 --> 02:28:09.220
Deputy Speaker Ferjenel G. Biron, M.D.: Year on year until today.

asr-002418
02:28:12.730 --> 02:28:15.990
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: We will provide po the data, Mr. Chair.

asr-002419
02:28:16.670 --> 02:28:20.030
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Kung year on year po, starting 2022.

asr-002420
02:28:20.030 --> 02:28:30.990
Deputy Speaker Ferjenel G. Biron, M.D.: Okay. So, Mr. Chair, I would like to request the DOH to furnish this committee and this representation a copy of those reports.

asr-002421
02:28:31.430 --> 02:28:39.030
Deputy Speaker Ferjenel G. Biron, M.D.: But while waiting for those reports, may I know from the good secretary, what are the reasons, where do you attribute...

asr-002422
02:28:39.970 --> 02:28:42.570
Deputy Speaker Ferjenel G. Biron, M.D.: this problem on expired medicines?

asr-002423
02:28:42.730 --> 02:28:47.450
Deputy Speaker Ferjenel G. Biron, M.D.: Kasi, this accounts for hundreds of millions since 2022.

asr-002424
02:28:48.630 --> 02:28:56.010
Deputy Speaker Ferjenel G. Biron, M.D.: Ang tanong is, is it attributed to poor procurement planning, inventory management control?

asr-002425
02:28:56.610 --> 02:28:58.050
Deputy Speaker Ferjenel G. Biron, M.D.: Where do you think is the problem?

asr-002426
02:28:58.050 --> 02:29:06.200
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: From my initial analysis po, given the three weeks that I was on the job,

asr-002427
02:29:06.720 --> 02:29:11.260
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: wala hong automated na talagang supply chain system.

asr-002428
02:29:11.260 --> 02:29:15.100
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: That already tracks stock level down to the level of the CHDs.

asr-002429
02:29:15.320 --> 02:29:20.440
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: It's all pen and paper, which we need to really improve on.

asr-002430
02:29:21.020 --> 02:29:27.460
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: But the other thing that we're looking at, given nga po na PhilHealth is expanding its coverage of gamot,

asr-002431
02:29:27.920 --> 02:29:32.960
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: some of the commodities can also be procured through the gamot program of PhilHealth.

asr-002432
02:29:33.420 --> 02:29:36.180
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Para rin wala pong double financing.

asr-002433
02:29:37.460 --> 02:29:41.080
Deputy Speaker Ferjenel G. Biron, M.D.: You mean to say, Mr. Secretary, hanggang ngayon walang operating software?

asr-002434
02:29:41.260 --> 02:29:42.500
Deputy Speaker Ferjenel G. Biron, M.D.: Ang warehouse ninyo?

asr-002435
02:29:43.760 --> 02:29:51.360
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Meron pong LMEIS, ito po ay donated, pero hindi po ganong kaganda ang feedback po sa atin.

asr-002436
02:29:53.200 --> 02:29:59.820
Deputy Speaker Ferjenel G. Biron, M.D.: So, all of these medicines procured in the central office get stocked in your central warehouse?

asr-002437
02:30:00.080 --> 02:30:06.320
Deputy Speaker Ferjenel G. Biron, M.D.: At tumatagal doon at hindi na dideliver sa central, sa CHDs, regional offices.

asr-002438
02:30:11.450 --> 02:30:23.470
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: So ang ginawa nga po ng ating bagong procurement undersecretary ay naggawa po ng sistema na bago po mag-procure o mag-bid out ng bagong mga commodities,

asr-002439
02:30:24.090 --> 02:30:28.270
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: ay inaalam po yung mga stock level doon sa iba't ibang region, kinoconsolidate.

asr-002440
02:30:28.690 --> 02:30:33.510
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: At pagsatansya po namin ay may sapat pa, hindi po muna gagawin yung procurement.

asr-002441
02:30:33.510 --> 02:30:43.870
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: That's one. Number two po ay yun nga, meron tayong electronic inventory system na kailangan po natin i-upgrade.

asr-002442
02:30:45.990 --> 02:30:55.190
Deputy Speaker Ferjenel G. Biron, M.D.: How much do you spend? How much does DOH spend on warehousing? What is the budget on warehousing and logistics annually, Mr. Secretary?

asr-002443
02:31:03.260 --> 02:31:11.580
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Ang supply chain management including warehousing and tracking po, last year was 1.2 billion.

asr-002444
02:31:11.580 --> 02:31:18.980
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: And for this year, approved NEP is 1.23. May konti pong increase ng 1.8%.

asr-002445
02:31:18.980 --> 02:31:25.520
Deputy Speaker Ferjenel G. Biron, M.D.: If you itemize the budget, how much goes to warehousing? How much goes to logistics?

asr-002446
02:31:25.520 --> 02:31:47.600
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Out of the 1.2 billion, give or take po, 250 or almost 1.4 or 1.5 is in warehousing, 15 million for electronics.

asr-002447
02:31:47.660 --> 02:31:53.020
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: And 90 million po for operating expense.

asr-002448
02:31:54.700 --> 02:32:06.840
Deputy Speaker Ferjenel G. Biron, M.D.: Given this huge budget for warehousing and logistics, does it make sense that most of your national program should be downloaded to the regions?

asr-002449
02:32:08.080 --> 02:32:14.820
Deputy Speaker Ferjenel G. Biron, M.D.: Regionalize ninyo ang mga national program kasi nangyayari is, pinoprocure ng central, hindi naman nadideliver sa region.

asr-002450
02:32:15.660 --> 02:32:17.640
Deputy Speaker Ferjenel G. Biron, M.D.: Katulad ng TB program ninyo.

asr-002451
02:32:17.660 --> 02:32:19.060
Deputy Speaker Ferjenel G. Biron, M.D.: HIV program ninyo.

asr-002452
02:32:19.120 --> 02:32:20.720
Deputy Speaker Ferjenel G. Biron, M.D.: Family planning program ninyo.

asr-002453
02:32:21.180 --> 02:32:25.820
Deputy Speaker Ferjenel G. Biron, M.D.: They all get stuck in the central warehouse without it being delivered to the regional offices.

asr-002454
02:32:26.560 --> 02:32:30.060
Deputy Speaker Ferjenel G. Biron, M.D.: Would you agree with me that it's now the time to regionalize procurement?

asr-002455
02:32:31.280 --> 02:32:37.920
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Yes, sir. In fact, we already are regionalizing. 60% of our commodities are actually procured at the region.

asr-002456
02:32:38.080 --> 02:32:41.300
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: These are the more commonly available meds.

asr-002457
02:32:41.300 --> 02:32:47.340
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Ang naka-centralized lang po talaga are the high-value medicines like cancer meds and vaccine.

asr-002458
02:32:47.660 --> 02:32:48.680
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Immunizations po.

asr-002459
02:32:49.080 --> 02:32:50.920
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: So 60% naman po nasa region.

asr-002460
02:32:51.420 --> 02:32:54.480
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Yung nabanggit ko pong warehousing, kasama din po doon ang regions.

asr-002461
02:32:56.480 --> 02:32:59.500
Deputy Speaker Ferjenel G. Biron, M.D.: So the cost of warehousing includes the other regions?

asr-002462
02:33:00.740 --> 02:33:02.020
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Includes na po the other regions.

asr-002463
02:33:02.840 --> 02:33:07.240
Deputy Speaker Ferjenel G. Biron, M.D.: Well, I will have other questions, Mr. Secretary, with respect to HVEP.

asr-002464
02:33:07.360 --> 02:33:09.780
Deputy Speaker Ferjenel G. Biron, M.D.: But let me move on to FDA.

asr-002465
02:33:10.740 --> 02:33:12.520
Deputy Speaker Ferjenel G. Biron, M.D.: Is DG Tanakin around?

asr-002466
02:33:12.520 --> 02:33:21.980
Deputy Speaker Ferjenel G. Biron, M.D.: May I ask the good Director General to respond to some questions?

asr-002467
02:33:26.880 --> 02:33:30.820
Deputy Speaker Ferjenel G. Biron, M.D.: DG, may problema ang FDA, no?

asr-002468
02:33:31.260 --> 02:33:36.680
Deputy Speaker Ferjenel G. Biron, M.D.: It's been a problem on registrations.

asr-002469
02:33:37.320 --> 02:33:42.960
Deputy Speaker Ferjenel G. Biron, M.D.: And I believe the only way to address this is to fully digitalize the FDA,

asr-002470
02:33:43.320 --> 02:33:46.400
Deputy Speaker Ferjenel G. Biron, M.D.: especially the CDRR and the Medical Device Division.

asr-002471
02:33:46.820 --> 02:33:50.060
Deputy Speaker Ferjenel G. Biron, M.D.: Can you elaborate on the budget that you want Congress to provide you?

asr-002472
02:33:53.000 --> 02:33:55.980
FDA OIC Director General Atty. Franklin Anthony M. Tabaquin IV: Thank you, Congressman Beron.

asr-002473
02:33:56.940 --> 02:33:57.880
FDA OIC Director General Atty. Franklin Anthony M. Tabaquin IV: Yes, sir.

asr-002474
02:33:59.120 --> 02:34:05.240
FDA OIC Director General Atty. Franklin Anthony M. Tabaquin IV: The FDA has always been complaining of the lack of personnel

asr-002475
02:34:05.240 --> 02:34:11.620
FDA OIC Director General Atty. Franklin Anthony M. Tabaquin IV: and the influx of the very high volume of applications.

asr-002476
02:34:12.560 --> 02:34:17.540
FDA OIC Director General Atty. Franklin Anthony M. Tabaquin IV: So what the CDRR thought of doing in collaboration with our other centers

asr-002477
02:34:17.540 --> 02:34:24.620
FDA OIC Director General Atty. Franklin Anthony M. Tabaquin IV: is to come up with a system, a digital system,

asr-002478
02:34:24.960 --> 02:34:27.540
FDA OIC Director General Atty. Franklin Anthony M. Tabaquin IV: whereby the applications will...

asr-002479
02:34:29.120 --> 02:34:33.380
FDA OIC Director General Atty. Franklin Anthony M. Tabaquin IV: whereby the applications will be processed or evaluated.

asr-002480
02:34:33.900 --> 02:34:37.540
FDA OIC Director General Atty. Franklin Anthony M. Tabaquin IV: So basically, it's an end-to-end digital system, sir.

asr-002481
02:34:38.120 --> 02:34:42.100
FDA OIC Director General Atty. Franklin Anthony M. Tabaquin IV: In terms of the budget, it will require about ₱217 million.

asr-002482
02:34:42.620 --> 02:34:44.180
FDA OIC Director General Atty. Franklin Anthony M. Tabaquin IV: That is the minimum estimate.

asr-002483
02:34:44.900 --> 02:34:49.160
FDA OIC Director General Atty. Franklin Anthony M. Tabaquin IV: This is not a program, a subscription-based program, sir.

asr-002484
02:34:49.640 --> 02:34:55.100
FDA OIC Director General Atty. Franklin Anthony M. Tabaquin IV: This will be an in-house program that is really designed for CDRR,

asr-002485
02:34:55.100 --> 02:34:58.500
FDA OIC Director General Atty. Franklin Anthony M. Tabaquin IV: which can hopefully be...

asr-002486
02:34:59.120 --> 02:35:01.620
FDA OIC Director General Atty. Franklin Anthony M. Tabaquin IV: also replicated by the other centers as well, sir.

asr-002487
02:35:02.840 --> 02:35:06.680
Deputy Speaker Ferjenel G. Biron, M.D.: What is the total budget that you are requesting Congress to provide you?

asr-002488
02:35:07.300 --> 02:35:12.860
FDA OIC Director General Atty. Franklin Anthony M. Tabaquin IV: The total budget just for the system, sir, is ₱217 million approximately.

asr-002489
02:35:12.860 --> 02:35:21.200
FDA OIC Director General Atty. Franklin Anthony M. Tabaquin IV: But the total MOOE that we would appeal, sir, is ₱517...

asr-002490
02:35:21.200 --> 02:35:21.600
FDA OIC Director General Atty. Franklin Anthony M. Tabaquin IV: I'm sorry.

asr-002491
02:35:27.840 --> 02:35:28.960
FDA OIC Director General Atty. Franklin Anthony M. Tabaquin IV: ₱589 million.

asr-002492
02:35:30.260 --> 02:35:33.260
Deputy Speaker Ferjenel G. Biron, M.D.: Yeah, ₱518 is the one that will be provided by Congress.

asr-002493
02:35:33.400 --> 02:35:38.420
Deputy Speaker Ferjenel G. Biron, M.D.: But what is the expected revenue from the retained income of FDA?

asr-002494
02:35:40.240 --> 02:35:40.960
Deputy Speaker Ferjenel G. Biron, M.D.: What again, sir?

asr-002495
02:35:42.180 --> 02:35:45.920
Deputy Speaker Ferjenel G. Biron, M.D.: ₱518 million is the one that will be provided by Congress in the GAA.

asr-002496
02:35:46.180 --> 02:35:46.560
FDA OIC Director General Atty. Franklin Anthony M. Tabaquin IV: Yes, sir.

asr-002497
02:35:46.680 --> 02:35:49.540
Deputy Speaker Ferjenel G. Biron, M.D.: So, but I'm sure that you have retained income

asr-002498
02:35:49.540 --> 02:35:52.540
Deputy Speaker Ferjenel G. Biron, M.D.: coming from the revenues generated by the agency.

asr-002499
02:35:52.980 --> 02:35:59.520
Deputy Speaker Ferjenel G. Biron, M.D.: How much is the counterpart of the revenue provided by the retention of your income?

asr-002500
02:35:59.920 --> 02:36:01.780
FDA OIC Director General Atty. Franklin Anthony M. Tabaquin IV: Based on our current record, sir,

asr-002501
02:36:01.860 --> 02:36:02.520
FDA OIC Director General Atty. Franklin Anthony M. Tabaquin IV: it's amounting to approximately...

asr-002502
02:36:03.400 --> 02:36:06.420
FDA OIC Director General Atty. Franklin Anthony M. Tabaquin IV: Approximately ₱2 billion, Your Honor.

asr-002503
02:36:07.020 --> 02:36:10.280
FDA OIC Director General Atty. Franklin Anthony M. Tabaquin IV: But under current system, sir,

asr-002504
02:36:10.280 --> 02:36:13.820
FDA OIC Director General Atty. Franklin Anthony M. Tabaquin IV: we don't have access to that retained income

asr-002505
02:36:13.820 --> 02:36:18.280
FDA OIC Director General Atty. Franklin Anthony M. Tabaquin IV: unless it's time that we are allowed to touch.

asr-002506
02:36:19.240 --> 02:36:27.820
FDA OIC Director General Atty. Franklin Anthony M. Tabaquin IV: That we are hoping that the ₱580 million will be allowed to get from that SAGF, sir.

asr-002507
02:36:28.340 --> 02:36:28.600
Deputy Speaker Ferjenel G. Biron, M.D.: Okay.

asr-002508
02:36:28.920 --> 02:36:33.280
Deputy Speaker Ferjenel G. Biron, M.D.: So, one more last question, Mr. Chairman.

asr-002509
02:36:33.400 --> 02:36:37.500
Deputy Speaker Ferjenel G. Biron, M.D.: So, your budget that you're asking Congress is from the date 18.

asr-002510
02:36:38.120 --> 02:36:41.880
Deputy Speaker Ferjenel G. Biron, M.D.: Presently, you are not in the position to tap the retained income

asr-002511
02:36:41.880 --> 02:36:45.520
Deputy Speaker Ferjenel G. Biron, M.D.: unless you submit to DBM your business plan.

asr-002512
02:36:45.640 --> 02:36:46.100
Deputy Speaker Ferjenel G. Biron, M.D.: Is that correct?

asr-002513
02:36:46.940 --> 02:36:47.580
FDA OIC Director General Atty. Franklin Anthony M. Tabaquin IV: Yes, Your Honor.

asr-002514
02:36:47.920 --> 02:36:51.520
FDA OIC Director General Atty. Franklin Anthony M. Tabaquin IV: But we have already, the previous DG, DG Teston,

asr-002515
02:36:51.860 --> 02:36:54.400
FDA OIC Director General Atty. Franklin Anthony M. Tabaquin IV: has already submitted the five-year development plan,

asr-002516
02:36:54.720 --> 02:36:57.820
FDA OIC Director General Atty. Franklin Anthony M. Tabaquin IV: which is one of the conditions for us to be able to...

asr-002517
02:36:57.820 --> 02:36:58.720
Deputy Speaker Ferjenel G. Biron, M.D.: Okay, thank you, DG.

asr-002518
02:36:58.720 --> 02:37:02.520
Deputy Speaker Ferjenel G. Biron, M.D.: Mr. Chair, I will reserve my other questions for Phil Wealth

asr-002519
02:37:02.520 --> 02:37:03.600
Deputy Speaker Ferjenel G. Biron, M.D.: in the second round.

asr-002520
02:37:03.720 --> 02:37:04.440
Deputy Speaker Ferjenel G. Biron, M.D.: Thank you, Mr. Chair.

asr-002521
02:37:04.740 --> 02:37:09.220
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: Maraming salamat, Deputy Speaker Ferge at Attorney Tabakin.

asr-002522
02:37:09.340 --> 02:37:10.100
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: Maraming salamat po.

asr-002523
02:37:10.100 --> 02:37:17.180
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: And DOH is requested to submit the data requested by DS Ferge,

asr-002524
02:37:17.360 --> 02:37:20.600
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: especially those on the expired medicine.

asr-002525
02:37:21.620 --> 02:37:25.820
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: Mr. Chair, if the Honorable Biron is willing,

asr-002526
02:37:25.980 --> 02:37:29.780
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: may I amend his motion that the list include not only expired,

asr-002527
02:37:29.940 --> 02:37:32.100
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: but also expiring and near-expiring medicines.

asr-002528
02:37:32.520 --> 02:37:35.180
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: So, moved, Mr. Chair.

asr-002529
02:37:35.300 --> 02:37:36.340
Deputy Speaker Ferjenel G. Biron, M.D.: Second, Mr. Chair.

asr-002530
02:37:36.440 --> 02:37:37.320
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: There is a motion.

asr-002531
02:37:37.580 --> 02:37:38.540
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: Julie seconded.

asr-002532
02:37:39.200 --> 02:37:40.480
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: The motion is approved.

asr-002533
02:37:41.340 --> 02:37:46.160
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: Please, DOH, pakisubmit po yung expired, expiring, and near-expiring.

asr-002534
02:37:47.040 --> 02:37:51.420
Deputy Speaker Ferjenel G. Biron, M.D.: Mr. Chair, that includes the entire regional offices as well.

asr-002535
02:37:51.560 --> 02:37:53.120
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: Okay, hanggang sa regional offices.

asr-002536
02:37:53.880 --> 02:37:54.680
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: Maraming salamat po.

asr-002537
02:37:55.860 --> 02:37:57.880
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: So, time check lang po.

asr-002538
02:37:58.180 --> 02:37:59.820
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: It's 12.09.

asr-002539
02:38:00.640 --> 02:38:02.500
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: So, I guess mamayang konti.

asr-002540
02:38:02.520 --> 02:38:04.940
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: Magkaroon lang tayo ng biobreak.

asr-002541
02:38:06.600 --> 02:38:10.580
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: And siguro working lunch na lang, if okay sa ating mga members.

asr-002542
02:38:11.560 --> 02:38:20.710
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: So, for now, we recognize Assistant Minority Leader, Sarah Elago.

asr-002543
02:38:21.730 --> 02:38:22.690
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: Please proceed, ma'am.

asr-002544
02:38:24.430 --> 02:38:30.070
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Mr. Chair, tungkol sa existing policies na kaugnay ng anti-hospital detention,

asr-002545
02:38:30.070 --> 02:38:35.390
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: may we know if the DOH has the numbers regarding the unsettled promissory notes,

asr-002546
02:38:35.690 --> 02:38:38.190
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: and the amount of collectibles from patients,

asr-002547
02:38:38.670 --> 02:38:40.590
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: lumalaki po ba ito over the years?

asr-002548
02:38:59.030 --> 02:39:03.110
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Mr. Chair, if you can just provide the detailed data, unfortunately.

asr-002549
02:39:03.510 --> 02:39:07.430
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: If it's okay with Congresswoman Sarah, okay lang po ba?

asr-002550
02:39:07.750 --> 02:39:08.670
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Yes, Mr. Chair.

asr-002551
02:39:09.410 --> 02:39:17.630
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Now, does the department have an active monitoring of the magnitude of foreclosed or ceased collateral

asr-002552
02:39:17.630 --> 02:39:20.390
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: because of these unsettled promissory notes?

asr-002553
02:39:20.890 --> 02:39:22.630
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Hingin po natin yung detalya, pero naistatis.

asr-002554
02:39:22.750 --> 02:39:23.570
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Hindi natin malaman.

asr-002555
02:39:23.670 --> 02:39:24.810
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Paano ba yung monitoring?

asr-002556
02:39:25.310 --> 02:39:29.970
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Paano natin natitiyak na kung may mga issues at concerns tungkol dito,

asr-002557
02:39:30.090 --> 02:39:31.790
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: ay nasasagot natin agad?

asr-002558
02:39:34.230 --> 02:39:40.750
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: So, as I mentioned earlier po, meron tayong parang action center, 1555.

asr-002559
02:39:41.550 --> 02:39:44.550
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Pero parang gusto nga naming palawigin,

asr-002560
02:39:44.550 --> 02:39:47.930
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: and together with Phil Health, really manage it professionally.

asr-002561
02:39:49.330 --> 02:39:53.750
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: So, yun po ay dinudulog doon, and then we have filled offices po to invest.

asr-002562
02:39:54.410 --> 02:39:54.890
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Investigate.

asr-002563
02:39:55.230 --> 02:39:58.910
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Because we also want to give due process to any complaints.

asr-002564
02:39:59.750 --> 02:40:05.130
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Mr. Chair, anong ibig sabihin for this action center to be managed by DOH professionally?

asr-002565
02:40:05.610 --> 02:40:07.710
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Ibig sabihin, is this service outsourced?

asr-002566
02:40:08.090 --> 02:40:13.890
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Or paano po ang management, administration, staffing, and funding for this particular action center?

asr-002567
02:40:16.500 --> 02:40:21.120
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: It's internally managed po, and limited pa lang yung seats.

asr-002568
02:40:21.120 --> 02:40:26.120
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Kaya nga po, my experience when I was in Phil Health, it's an outsourced service.

asr-002569
02:40:26.200 --> 02:40:34.080
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: And we get good statistics and reports, drop calls, how many are resolved, what are the most common complaints.

asr-002570
02:40:35.220 --> 02:40:41.720
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: And then there are escalation also on kailan iyaakyat, can it be resolved at the level of the call center agent,

asr-002571
02:40:42.040 --> 02:40:47.580
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: when it will be brought up to the level of the regional directors, and even all the way up to central office.

asr-002572
02:40:48.000 --> 02:40:49.520
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: So, yun po yung ating pag-aaral.

asr-002573
02:40:50.520 --> 02:40:56.180
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Mr. Chair, kunin natin yung detalye ng mga naitawag na ilapit ng mga concerns dito sa action center.

asr-002574
02:40:56.180 --> 02:41:00.560
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Kung ano yung nature ng mga concerns ng mga tumatawag.

asr-002575
02:41:00.940 --> 02:41:09.560
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Natanong ko rin ito dahil maraming ospital, lalo na sa private hospitals na sapin-sapin ang dinaranas na pananamantala at hinagpis ng mga pasyente

asr-002576
02:41:09.560 --> 02:41:14.520
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: dahil sa mga kondisyon sa pagbabayad ng kanilang balanse sa hospital bills.

asr-002577
02:41:14.920 --> 02:41:24.900
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: At tulad ng pasyente, paano po kung walang pwedeng maikolateral na lupa o bahay yung mga pasyente, saan po sila maaaring lumapit sa ganitong mga kondisyon?

asr-002578
02:41:24.900 --> 02:41:26.160
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: At pinapayagan.

asr-002579
02:41:26.180 --> 02:41:34.460
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: At pinapayagan ba ng DOH itong pagpapataw ng mga pagkataas-taas po na compound interest rate sa mga kolateral?

asr-002580
02:41:46.600 --> 02:41:50.480
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Yung compounding po, wala pa pong policy.

asr-002581
02:41:50.680 --> 02:41:56.900
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Pero yung pong physical detention, yun po yung maliitong set rules.

asr-002582
02:41:57.040 --> 02:42:03.060
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Kasi parang commercial terms po yun that is entered into between the patient and the hospital.

asr-002583
02:42:03.540 --> 02:42:10.250
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Sir Chair, may batas din po tayo na anti-hospital detention.

asr-002584
02:42:10.330 --> 02:42:14.750
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: At kinakailangan talaga ma-review na yung implementation na ito.

asr-002585
02:42:14.910 --> 02:42:24.450
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Because while it is true that RA 9439 allows these kinds of arrangements, it is an injustice to let things remain the same.

asr-002586
02:42:24.770 --> 02:42:29.750
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Sa halit po nabalansihin yung interest ng tubo sa mga ospital at na mga pasyente,

asr-002587
02:42:29.930 --> 02:42:35.370
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: ang dapat po natin makonsidera ay ang paglalaan ng higit pang pondo sa mga pampublikong ospital

asr-002588
02:42:35.370 --> 02:42:39.630
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: na sa gayon maging sapat ang mga facilities, ang kanilang bed capacity,

asr-002589
02:42:39.630 --> 02:42:43.630
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: para sa mas marami nating mga nangangailangan ng mga kababayan.

asr-002590
02:42:44.590 --> 02:42:48.950
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: At nagiging problema din po ito pag privatize talaga yung healthcare in general,

asr-002591
02:42:49.330 --> 02:42:56.630
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: wherein we hide under the cloak of balancing interest while profiteering from supposed social services are actually left unchecked.

asr-002592
02:42:57.610 --> 02:43:01.710
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Kaugnay nito, Mr. Chair, lahat po ng mga lumapit din sa atin ng mga kaso,

asr-002593
02:43:01.930 --> 02:43:05.130
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: kaugnay nito ay isusumitin natin sa DOH.

asr-002594
02:43:05.210 --> 02:43:07.710
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Sunod naman po, nais kong magtanong,

asr-002595
02:43:09.630 --> 02:43:31.240
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: ang aditong nakalaan para sa Family Planning and Reproductive Health ay P664 million for 2020-7.

asr-002596
02:43:32.580 --> 02:43:44.360
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Mr. Chair, kaugnay nito, pwedeng makuha natin yung breakdown nitong P9.1 billion para sa Family Health, Immunization, Nutrition, and Responsible Parenting.

asr-002597
02:43:44.360 --> 02:43:46.620
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Nabanggit na po yung para sa RH.

asr-002598
02:43:47.340 --> 02:43:49.780
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Nabanggit na po yung ibang sub-programs sa ilalim nito.

asr-002599
02:43:50.660 --> 02:43:51.980
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: We can provide po.

asr-002600
02:43:52.340 --> 02:43:59.300
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: There's a list po on commodities, on women and children's protection, on safe motherhood,

asr-002601
02:43:59.800 --> 02:44:02.980
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: on adolescent health program, on family planning program support.

asr-002602
02:44:03.100 --> 02:44:04.520
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: We can give po the breakdown.

asr-002603
02:44:06.100 --> 02:44:10.480
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Mr. Chair, ahingin po natin yung detalye ng proposal, kaugnay nyan.

asr-002604
02:44:10.480 --> 02:44:14.760
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Pagdating naman sa women and children protection units,

asr-002605
02:44:14.860 --> 02:44:17.320
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: magkano yung gagastusin natin?

asr-002606
02:44:17.340 --> 02:44:23.380
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: At may plano ba na magsagawa, mag-establish pa ng mas marami nito sa buong bansa?

asr-002607
02:44:24.760 --> 02:44:34.540
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: So, meron po tayong nakalaan na P51 million for women and children's protection support to women and children's protection unit in P51 hospitals po.

asr-002608
02:44:37.140 --> 02:44:42.980
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Sa P51 hospitals, may plano po tayo for next year na funding for establishment of new ones?

asr-002609
02:44:42.980 --> 02:44:46.660
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: Pano magkano exista?

asr-002610
02:44:48.820 --> 02:44:50.680
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Yung P51, Mr. Chair?

asr-002611
02:44:50.700 --> 02:44:53.120
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Sir, is inclusive already of the expansion.

asr-002612
02:44:53.880 --> 02:44:58.060
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: I just, I'm asking how much is the current number?

asr-002613
02:44:59.220 --> 02:45:00.080
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Mr. Chair, kasama

asr-002614
02:45:00.080 --> 02:45:27.260
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: rin ba sa P51M yung pagpupondo sa development at distribution ng Sexual Assault Investigation Kit na sariling gawa po ng mga Pilipino, yan ho ay isa sa mga tagumpay ng mga DOST-backed projects natin para magkaroon ng science-backed support services para sa access to justice ng mga nabibiktima ng abuso.

asr-002615
02:45:27.260 --> 02:45:45.120
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Yung P51M po ay kasama na yung kits although medyo we need data nga to see if it is sufficient kasi nga baka dun pa lang sa support ng program.

asr-002616
02:45:45.240 --> 02:45:55.880
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: We will provide po makano po yung actual breakdown po nitong P51M for Women and Child Protection to include po kung makano yung kits.

asr-002617
02:45:55.880 --> 02:45:59.960
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: At the other ones are to support the operation.

asr-002618
02:45:59.960 --> 02:46:05.580
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Yung kits po ay kukunin natin yung na-develop ng DOST. O meron po kayong ibang source?

asr-002619
02:46:17.560 --> 02:46:30.060
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Hindi pa po explicit Mr. Chair na yung DOST-developed kits ang ginagamit but we will review po kasi we can incorporate that in our TOR.

asr-002620
02:46:31.120 --> 02:46:36.900
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Yes, Mr. Chair. Napaka-ganda ko nung dinevelop mismo ng atin.

asr-002621
02:46:36.920 --> 02:46:45.040
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: At yung mga siyentistang Pilipino at dapat yung DOH yung manguna sa paggamit nito sa mga WCPUs natin sa buong bansa.

asr-002622
02:46:45.520 --> 02:47:01.100
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Dahil yan ho ang dilema ngayon ng DOST, meron ho tayong magandang na-develop na saikit pero ang DOH po sa ngayon ay wala pa ho malinaw na plano para mag-procure ng diretsyo at tumulong sa distribution nito para ho sa buong bansa.

asr-002623
02:47:01.100 --> 02:47:06.420
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Ngayon naman, Mr. Chair, tungkol sa Cancer Assistance Fund, lumaki ho ito ng lubusan.

asr-002624
02:47:06.920 --> 02:47:17.140
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Meron po tayong House Resolution para tignan kung paano na ba ang implementation ngayon ng ating National Integrated Cancer Control Program.

asr-002625
02:47:17.460 --> 02:47:33.640
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: At isa po sa mga pinakalalapit na concerns sa representasyon na ito ay yung kulang na suporta para sa post-treatment, aftercare, survivorship benefits and other support services.

asr-002626
02:47:33.640 --> 02:47:36.640
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Sa ngayon po ba ang PhilHealth ba na expanded?

asr-002627
02:47:36.920 --> 02:47:47.380
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Sa ngayon po ba yung package natin para sa cancer care mas malawak po yung ating masasagot na mga serbisyo?

asr-002628
02:47:47.380 --> 02:48:05.820
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: At ngayon din sa DOH, kasama na po ba dito sa pagtaas ng ating Cancer Assistance Fund, lahat po ng care-related components na kailangan ng ating mga pasyente at lahat po ng ating mga cancer warriors at survivors?

asr-002629
02:48:06.920 --> 02:48:09.700
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: Okay. Please respond.

asr-002630
02:48:10.060 --> 02:48:21.640
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: For the Cancer Fund nga po, meron kaming minumungkahing mga amendments to include po and expand the coverage including blood products, even the nutritional support.

asr-002631
02:48:21.900 --> 02:48:36.760
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Kasi yung initial po medyo limited lang to medicine. So kaya po this year, tumaas po yung ating Cancer Fund ng almost 25.6% to account all those additional support po.

asr-002632
02:48:36.920 --> 02:48:48.800
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Okay. To end, Mr. Chair, I'd just like to put on record a request for the DOH to submit to this committee its report on its gender and development mandate compliance.

asr-002633
02:48:49.380 --> 02:48:56.380
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: That's one. Number two po yung tungkol sa pagpapatupad natin ng National HIV Policy Act sa RH.

asr-002634
02:48:56.800 --> 02:49:03.020
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Gayon din po sa programa natin para sa National Integrated Cancer Control Program.

asr-002635
02:49:03.540 --> 02:49:04.720
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Maraming salamat, Mr. Chair.

asr-002636
02:49:04.720 --> 02:49:06.900
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: Okay. Maraming salamat, Assistant.

asr-002637
02:49:06.920 --> 02:49:08.900
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: I'm Assistant Minority Leader, Sarah Ilago.

asr-002638
02:49:09.660 --> 02:49:18.460
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: And DOH is requested to submit said documents to the committee para ma-share po natin sa ating mga membro.

asr-002639
02:49:19.020 --> 02:49:23.580
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: If I may, Chair, also the anti-detention data po, nirequested po.

asr-002640
02:49:23.960 --> 02:49:24.960
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: Okay. Thank you.

asr-002641
02:49:25.500 --> 02:49:27.480
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: So now we go back to the majority.

