Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Yung una po yung PhilHealth kasi nga po, based on our projection of the actual benefit payment for indirect members,

asr-002676
02:52:09.050 --> 02:52:10.050
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: ay kulang.

asr-002677
02:52:10.130 --> 02:52:14.810
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Yung una po yung 53, 73, 74 na binigay.

asr-002678
02:52:14.930 --> 02:52:19.130
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Ang initial projection po ay 244.

asr-002679
02:52:19.470 --> 02:52:20.150
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: So, isa po yun.

asr-002680
02:52:20.590 --> 02:52:21.810
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Pangalwa po yung HVEP.

asr-002681
02:52:22.010 --> 02:52:22.970
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: What again?

asr-002682
02:52:23.050 --> 02:52:23.590
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: How much again?

asr-002683
02:52:24.190 --> 02:52:29.210
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: The projected po is about 244.

asr-002684
02:52:29.810 --> 02:52:38.030
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Yet, we're only given to cover the benefit payment of the indirect member, 74.

asr-002685
02:52:38.030 --> 02:52:40.030
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: So, a difference of almost...

asr-002686
02:52:40.130 --> 02:52:42.130
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Yes, 170.

asr-002687
02:52:42.130 --> 02:52:43.130
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Yes, 170.

asr-002688
02:52:43.130 --> 02:52:48.130
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: So, you are us requesting with Beverly, President Beverly, can we hear you?

asr-002689
02:52:48.130 --> 02:52:50.130
PhilHealth President and CEO Dr. Beverly Lorraine Ho: Yes, sir.

asr-002690
02:52:50.130 --> 02:53:00.130
PhilHealth President and CEO Dr. Beverly Lorraine Ho: So, as mentioned earlier, in the past, our estimate was based on headcounts and proposed premium per headcount.

asr-002691
02:53:00.130 --> 02:53:03.130
PhilHealth President and CEO Dr. Beverly Lorraine Ho: That should be around 376.

asr-002692
02:53:03.130 --> 02:53:06.130
PhilHealth President and CEO Dr. Beverly Lorraine Ho: So, that was our original proposal.

asr-002693
02:53:06.130 --> 02:53:08.130
PhilHealth President and CEO Dr. Beverly Lorraine Ho: I guess we recognize.

asr-002694
02:53:08.130 --> 02:53:10.130
PhilHealth President and CEO Dr. Beverly Lorraine Ho: It's measurable.

asr-002695
02:53:10.130 --> 02:53:11.130
PhilHealth President and CEO Dr. Beverly Lorraine Ho: Malaki po talaga.

asr-002696
02:53:11.130 --> 02:53:20.130
PhilHealth President and CEO Dr. Beverly Lorraine Ho: So, if we just look at the parang break-even point, our expected benefit payout for indirect contributor next year is 244 billion.

asr-002697
02:53:21.130 --> 02:53:25.130
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: How much are you requesting the committee to restore?

asr-002698
02:53:25.130 --> 02:53:28.380
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Something reasonable.

asr-002699
02:53:28.380 --> 02:53:34.380
PhilHealth President and CEO Dr. Beverly Lorraine Ho: Sir, it's 170 additional just to get us to break-even point.

asr-002700
02:53:34.380 --> 02:53:39.380
PhilHealth President and CEO Dr. Beverly Lorraine Ho: And that's even assuming it's the same rate of utilization this year.

asr-002701
02:53:39.380 --> 02:53:40.380
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Thank you.

asr-002702
02:53:40.380 --> 02:53:43.380
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Thank you for your program for mental health.

asr-002703
02:53:43.380 --> 02:53:48.380
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Again, the oral suffers very much in mental health because we have no practitioners.

asr-002704
02:53:48.380 --> 02:53:50.380
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: We have no doctors there on mental health.

asr-002705
02:53:50.380 --> 02:53:54.380
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: So, kindly look at this how PhilHealth will be able to help us.

asr-002706
02:53:54.380 --> 02:53:56.380
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Thank you once again.

asr-002707
02:53:56.380 --> 02:54:01.380
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Secretary Edwin, what else, aside from PhilHealth, are your priority requests?

asr-002708
02:54:01.380 --> 02:54:09.380
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: The next, po, is the Health Facilities Enhancement Program, or HFEP, because we want local governments to really be sustainable.

asr-002709
02:54:09.380 --> 02:54:15.380
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Para po hindi lahat umakit sa apex nating hospital sa region na overload po eh.

asr-002710
02:54:15.380 --> 02:54:20.380
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: So, to really equip them, we requested 19 billion.

asr-002711
02:54:20.380 --> 02:54:22.380
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: We were given only 14.5.

asr-002712
02:54:22.380 --> 02:54:26.380
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: So, ang shortfall po ay 15.1 billion po.

asr-002713
02:54:26.380 --> 02:54:27.380
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: How much?

asr-002714
02:54:27.380 --> 02:54:28.380
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: 15 point.

asr-002715
02:54:28.380 --> 02:54:32.380
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: 15.1 billion po yung ating shortfall.

asr-002716
02:54:32.380 --> 02:54:35.380
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: 29 po yung hininge, 14.5 po ang naibigay.

asr-002717
02:54:35.380 --> 02:54:37.380
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Yeah, we agree that we have to focus on the facilities.

asr-002718
02:54:37.380 --> 02:54:42.380
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: We have to focus on the facilities, Health Facilities Enhancement Program.

asr-002719
02:54:42.380 --> 02:54:45.380
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: HFEP, it helps really our rural areas.

asr-002720
02:54:45.380 --> 02:54:46.380
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Correct po.

asr-002721
02:54:46.380 --> 02:54:49.380
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: To be able to meet the health requirements.

asr-002722
02:54:49.380 --> 02:54:51.380
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: So, that is 15 billion.

asr-002723
02:54:51.380 --> 02:54:52.380
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Thank you.

asr-002724
02:54:52.380 --> 02:54:56.380
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: What else would you need to request?

