asr-002740
02:56:09.260 --> 02:56:10.260
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Thank you, Mr. Chairman.

asr-002741
02:56:10.260 --> 02:56:11.260
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: So, that will be...

asr-002742
02:56:11.260 --> 02:56:14.260
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: We should try to help restore that.

asr-002743
02:56:14.260 --> 02:56:16.260
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: So, now I have some questions.

asr-002744
02:56:16.260 --> 02:56:33.250
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: How much is the country's essential medicine supply can local pharmaceutical manufacturers currently sustain during another pandemic or major import disruption?

asr-002745
02:56:33.250 --> 02:56:40.610
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Talking of supply from the local pharmaceutical manufacturers.

asr-002746
02:56:40.610 --> 02:56:50.210
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: The first line essential medicines po are mostly in the gamot package,

asr-002747
02:56:50.210 --> 02:56:53.210
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: which are mostly sourced locally po.

asr-002748
02:56:53.210 --> 02:57:03.210
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Although we also provide support to lalo na po yung mga GIDA areas and third, fourth, fifth class municipalities,

asr-002749
02:57:03.210 --> 02:57:06.210
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: but these are sourced locally po.

asr-002750
02:57:06.210 --> 02:57:07.210
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Thank you.

asr-002751
02:57:07.210 --> 02:57:19.210
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: And your integrated roadmap for the Philippine pharmaceutical industry targets local capacity to produce 60% of the country's registered medicines by 2030.

asr-002752
02:57:19.210 --> 02:57:21.210
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: How is that going along?

asr-002753
02:57:21.210 --> 02:57:42.720
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: From my understanding po is we have incentives for local manufacturers to locate in Clark because we already identified a pharmacy free port or tax-free arrangement in the export processing zone in Clark.

asr-002754
02:57:42.720 --> 02:57:52.720
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: But I think this is being headed by DTI together, I think, with the UP Manila.

asr-002755
02:57:52.720 --> 02:57:56.720
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: But parang konti pa po yung naglo-locate eh.

asr-002756
02:57:56.720 --> 02:58:01.720
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: So, we would like to also look into how we can further incentivize.

asr-002757
02:58:01.720 --> 02:58:10.720
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Probably align also the FDA to also expedite the licensing and approval of local manufacturers.

asr-002758
02:58:10.720 --> 02:58:19.720
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Yeah, my main point, Mr. Chairman, is to be able to encourage and support our local manufactured medicines.

asr-002759
02:58:19.720 --> 02:58:20.720
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: And so, following the mandate of the Philippine pharmaceutical industry, I think we need to do that.

asr-002760
02:58:20.720 --> 02:58:21.720
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Thank you.

asr-002761
02:58:21.720 --> 02:58:28.720
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Following the mandate of the TAC-Pinoy Act, and then of course, still compliant with the New Government Procurement Act.

asr-002762
02:58:28.720 --> 02:58:35.720
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: So, how will the country and our hospitals build local capacity before the next possible supplier pricing crisis?

asr-002763
02:58:35.720 --> 02:58:47.920
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Yun nga po, yung essential drug list na kailangan pong pag-aralan at tingnan kung pwede ma-expand.

asr-002764
02:58:47.920 --> 02:58:53.920
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Then secondly po, we're activating the Price Negotiation Board, which is also mandated in the UHC,

asr-002765
02:58:53.920 --> 02:59:04.920
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: which PhilHealth and DOH combined can also at least do market signaling to be able to negotiate.

asr-002766
02:59:04.920 --> 02:59:12.920
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: And given the current increase in gamot utilization plus the actual purchases of DOH,

asr-002767
02:59:12.920 --> 02:59:18.920
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: that's a substantial volume to actually negotiate the price.

asr-002768
02:59:18.920 --> 02:59:22.920
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Also, we are looking at, again, the multiple drug.

asr-002769
02:59:23.920 --> 02:59:24.920
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Anong tawag mo dun?

asr-002770
02:59:24.920 --> 02:59:30.200
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Yung entry para may market friction, yung multiple players.

asr-002771
02:59:30.200 --> 02:59:41.200
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: For the FDA to also look into allowing multiple suppliers of certain essential drugs to create some market dynamics.

asr-002772
02:59:41.200 --> 02:59:42.200
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Thank you.

asr-002773
02:59:42.200 --> 02:59:53.860
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Does the Secretary therefore commit, during your term, that you also give very much support to the local manufacturers of medicine?

asr-002774
02:59:53.860 --> 02:59:54.860
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Yes, definitely po.

asr-002775
02:59:54.860 --> 02:59:55.860
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Thank you very much.

