Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Ito po yung report na inquirer, sa health index, sa health care index po, ang Pilipinas po ay number 87 out of 110 countries.

asr-002897
03:58:33.680 --> 03:58:36.580
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Bukod po dyan, compared to other countries, dito sa...

asr-002898
03:58:37.280 --> 03:58:37.580
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Dito sa...

asr-002899
03:58:38.160 --> 03:58:44.160
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Southeast Asia, yung tatlong bansa na lang po, Thailand, Indonesia, and the Philippines.

asr-002900
03:58:44.160 --> 03:58:53.760
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Pag ikukumpara nyo po, yung sa GDP, 2.3% lang yung government ng contribution sa health care system.

asr-002901
03:58:53.880 --> 03:58:59.400
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: 2.3% of the 512 billion dollars na GDP natin.

asr-002902
03:59:00.040 --> 03:59:08.140
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Samantalang ang Thailand po, umaabot ng 4%, may git, ng GDP.

asr-002903
03:59:08.160 --> 03:59:23.220
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Ang GDP nila, o 560 billion dollars, ang Indonesia po, although 2% lang, yung GDP nila, yung para sa health care, eh 1.5 trillion naman yung kanilang GDP.

asr-002904
03:59:24.000 --> 03:59:29.400
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: So, paano ninyo aabutin itong pangarap na ito kung wala naman kayong pondo?

asr-002905
03:59:30.040 --> 03:59:40.400
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: So, Mr. Chair, Madam Chair, ang ano nga po, 8 to 10% nga po,

asr-002906
03:59:40.840 --> 03:59:46.000
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: ang percentage ng GDP, if we include the out-of-pocket or the private spending,

asr-002907
03:59:46.140 --> 03:59:52.660
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: ito pong, I think, nabanggit na nasa 2% is only the percentage of government spending and GDP.

asr-002908
03:59:52.960 --> 03:59:57.200
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: But, Secretary, kasi po mahirap na hasahan natin yung private spending.

asr-002909
