DOH HHRDB Director IV Johanna Solon S. Banzon, RN, MScIH, DTMPH: Just to say po that DOH and CHED has actually entered into an agreement so that DOH is able to share with CHED the lack in terms of education, in terms of the professionals that we need in the health sector so that the production of our health workers is actually according to our needs.

asr-004237
05:17:21.160 --> 05:17:22.620
DOH HHRDB Director IV Johanna Solon S. Banzon, RN, MScIH, DTMPH: Maraming salamat po, Madam Chair.

asr-004238
05:17:23.300 --> 05:17:45.620
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Madam Chair, if I may add, with the progression of our universal healthcare and there are now HEPNs being established and there is income generated out of PhilHealth, out of the second line, MAIFIP, we're thinking that there will be more revenues coming in that can be used to incentivize healthcare workers.

asr-004239
05:17:45.620 --> 05:17:52.900
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: And also in the long term because there is no more options in terms of career progression na hindi lang clinical yung focus.

asr-004240
05:17:53.300 --> 05:17:56.640
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: But can even be a manager of a whole healthcare system.

asr-004241
05:17:57.160 --> 05:18:08.020
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: I hope that would entice the healthcare workers to really stay on and look at the Philippines as a viable option long term.

asr-004242
