05:18:17.580 --> 05:18:21.980
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Thank you very much, Madam Chair.

asr-004246
05:18:22.160 --> 05:18:24.580
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: And good afternoon to the Department of Health.

asr-004247
05:18:24.580 --> 05:18:31.400
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: And especially to its new leadership that in the past two months I assumed their term.

asr-004248
05:18:31.920 --> 05:18:33.960
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: I'll go straight ahead na po.

asr-004249
05:18:34.720 --> 05:18:43.840
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Yung isang malaking issue ng kabataan at yung kalusugan nila ay yung kalusugang pangkaisipan or mental health.

asr-004250
05:18:43.840 --> 05:18:51.580
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: At ang napansin naman po natin ay nagkaroon po ng budget cut sa pag-aalaga ng mental health.

asr-004251
05:18:51.580 --> 05:18:58.220
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Under the National Expenditure Program's allocation for the Department of Health.

asr-004252
05:18:58.520 --> 05:19:06.580
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: In particular po, meron pong P311.49 million peso budget cut to MOOE ng NCMH.

asr-004253
05:19:07.220 --> 05:19:08.520
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: That's 21%.

asr-004254
05:19:08.520 --> 05:19:14.800
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: So given po na may estimated 12.5 million Filipinos that live with mental health conditions,

asr-004255
05:19:14.800 --> 05:19:20.800
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: ano po ba yung rational and even ano po yung na-cut dito sa...

asr-004256
05:19:21.580 --> 05:19:26.100
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: P311.49 million peso budget cut ng NCMH.

asr-004257
05:19:26.240 --> 05:19:26.660
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Madam Chair.

asr-004258
05:19:27.120 --> 05:19:52.070
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Madam Chair, this is along the line nga po ng pagbabawas po ng MOOE.

asr-004259
05:19:52.730 --> 05:19:58.930
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: So ang MOOE po ng National Center for Mental Health nga po ay...

asr-004260
05:19:58.930 --> 05:20:04.370
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Madam Chair, may we request the resource person to speak closer to the mic.

asr-004261
05:20:05.310 --> 05:20:05.910
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Thank you.

asr-004262
05:20:08.070 --> 05:20:09.930
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: So gaya po kanina na...

asr-004263
05:20:10.230 --> 05:20:15.470
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Napakita rin ni Representative Tino yung pagkakat po ng MOOE.

asr-004264
05:20:17.130 --> 05:20:20.950
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Ang sabi nga po namin, magbibigay kami ng report kung bakit po nag-cut.

asr-004265
05:20:22.290 --> 05:20:27.930
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Talaga po across the board, most of the DOH hospitals, MOOE budget was cut.

asr-004266
05:20:30.130 --> 05:20:32.510
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Kanina po over lunch, we were also talking.

asr-004267
05:20:32.510 --> 05:20:36.370
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Baka po kasi yung na-reallocate noong 2025.

asr-004268
05:20:37.110 --> 05:20:39.510
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: From the DPWH to...

asr-004269
05:20:40.230 --> 05:20:42.970
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: DOH, can be the reason.

asr-004270
05:20:43.090 --> 05:20:45.830
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Kaya umakyat po noong 2026.

asr-004271
05:20:46.030 --> 05:20:50.210
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Kaya nga po yung 2027, parang it's back to the usual normal.

asr-004272
05:20:50.390 --> 05:20:53.790
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: So we will need to compare with 2023, 2024.

asr-004273
05:20:54.250 --> 05:20:57.630
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: But we will provide po the exact data and the reason po.

asr-004274
05:20:58.290 --> 05:21:02.730
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Although ang pansin din naman po natin, even though may spike last year,

asr-004275
05:21:03.270 --> 05:21:08.790
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: the National Mental Health Budget has been reduced by half every year since 2025.

asr-004276
05:21:09.030 --> 05:21:10.070
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: From 1.5 billion...

asr-004277
05:21:10.230 --> 05:21:13.130
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: to significantly smaller allocations.

asr-004278
05:21:13.610 --> 05:21:22.630
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: And siguro ang tanong natin, dahil may push in legislation na magkaroon at mag-focus more on community-based mental health services.

asr-004279
05:21:23.330 --> 05:21:25.110
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: And we see that downward trend.

asr-004280
05:21:25.110 --> 05:21:39.110
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Ano po ba yung mga mental health services or efforts na isentro sa community yung pag-aalaga dito na pinupondohan ngayon ng DOH?

asr-004281
05:21:40.230 --> 05:21:45.030
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: And can I ask, may personal po ba na maaari pong tumutok dito?

asr-004282
05:21:46.050 --> 05:21:49.450
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Whether that is under PS or sa MOE, etc.

asr-004283
05:21:54.970 --> 05:22:03.830
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: All the health workers, especially the nurses, are capacitated by our MHGAP trained staff.

asr-004284
05:22:04.490 --> 05:22:10.290
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: And then we are also putting up our NCMH crisis hotline 24-7.

asr-004285
05:22:10.290 --> 05:22:14.290
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: And then there will be a medical access program.

asr-004286
05:22:14.870 --> 05:22:17.650
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Across 1,296 sites.

asr-004287
05:22:18.390 --> 05:22:22.230
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Or mostly, almost 64% of the cities and municipalities.

asr-004288
05:22:23.290 --> 05:22:27.210
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: And then PhilHealth nga po is also expanding its mental health program.

asr-004289
05:22:27.850 --> 05:22:35.150
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Kaya nga po yung aming interface is with settings-based impanelment,

asr-004290
05:22:35.310 --> 05:22:38.050
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: mostly, especially in schools.

asr-004291
05:22:38.690 --> 05:22:44.610
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: We will already coordinate with PhilHealth para po yung mental health program natin ma-augment.

asr-004292
05:22:44.870 --> 05:22:47.390
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Apart from what DOH is providing po.

asr-004293
05:22:48.190 --> 05:22:51.750
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: May I ask po, Madam Chair, ilang years na po yung NCMH hotline?

asr-004294
05:22:52.130 --> 05:22:59.690
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: At may napansin po ba tayong increase in the number of calls and the types of calls na trigger warning po,

asr-004295
05:22:59.750 --> 05:23:04.230
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: tungkol po sa suicide in the past years?

asr-004296
05:23:05.730 --> 05:23:06.930
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Or this year?

asr-004297
05:23:07.250 --> 05:23:19.640
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: So since 2019 po, ang cumulative call po natin ay 77,000.

asr-004298
05:23:20.340 --> 05:23:21.640
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: At nakikita po natin yung...

asr-004299
05:23:22.580 --> 05:23:27.980
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Medyo trend from 3,000 noong 2019, 11,000 noong 2020,

asr-004300
05:23:28.740 --> 05:23:33.920
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: 21,000 po noong 2021, at 18,000 noong 2022.

asr-004301
05:23:34.220 --> 05:23:35.700
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Yun po yung kasagsagan ng COVID.

asr-004302
05:23:36.540 --> 05:23:41.300
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Tapos po, nag-continue po yung trend noong 2023, 16,000.

asr-004303
05:23:41.400 --> 05:23:44.060
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: And noong 2024 po, 23,000.

asr-004304
05:23:44.060 --> 05:23:50.980
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: So if you would look at it, talagang po merong trend of increasing calls dito sa ating hotlines po.

asr-004305
05:23:52.580 --> 05:24:02.780
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: And may enough personnel po ba na-assign sa hotline or even yung magte-take on ng cases para po kung may mga natatanggap pong mga calls?

asr-004306
05:24:04.780 --> 05:24:06.760
